  partName: Left Front Sensor (2)
  description: The Left Front Sensor (2) is a tiny, elongated sensor positioned at
    the middle-left-front of the engine, responsible for monitoring various engine
    parameters such as temperature, pressure, or speed. This sensor provides critical
    data to the engine control unit, enabling it to make adjustments for optimal
    performance. Notably, the sensor's elongated shape allows it to be mounted in
    a compact space, minimizing its impact on the engine's overall geometry.
